    <!-- ===== 數據來源 (plan §13) ===== -->
    <string name="sources_title">Where the numbers come from</string>
    <string name="sources_intro">Every number in DeFAT has a stated source. This page says where each one comes from and how far to trust it.</string>
    <string name="sources_bmr_title">Basal metabolic rate (BMR)</string>
    <string name="sources_bmr_body">BMR is the energy your body uses at rest. When your body fat percentage is known, DeFAT uses Katch-McArdle. Otherwise it uses Henry / Oxford (2005). Using the Henry equations was the trainer\'s professional decision. No published study has compared them with Mifflin-St Jeor in a Chinese population yet, so treat the result as an estimate.</string>
    <string name="sources_tdee_title">Daily energy use (TDEE)</string>
    <string name="sources_tdee_body">TDEE is your BMR multiplied by the activity level you chose, which already includes your usual training. On days with logged exercise, DeFAT takes the higher of two calculations, so the same workout is never counted twice.</string>
    <string name="sources_food_title">Food numbers</string>
    <string name="sources_food_body">The official government food database could not be reached when this library was built, and the public lists we found disagree with each other by up to double. So every food is tagged: Approx. (standard composition values), Estimate (press or dietitian figures) or Trainer (the trainer\'s own numbers). The trainer\'s numbers replace all the others.</string>
    <string name="sources_water_title">Water suggestion</string>
    <string name="sources_water_body">The daily water suggestion is 35 ml for every kg of bodyweight, rounded down to the nearest 100 ml and never below 1,500 ml. It is a coaching rule of thumb, not a medical target.</string>
    <string name="sources_days_title">When a day starts</string>
    <string name="sources_days_body">A day starts at 04:00 unless you change it on the Me tab. A meal logged before that time counts towards the previous day. Changing the time moves no saved record; it only changes how days are grouped.</string>
    <string name="sources_disclaimer_heading">Medical disclaimer</string>

